cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "pulsebench: an evaluation protocol for seasonal, imbalanced time-series classification"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
abstract: >-
  pulsebench packages four evaluation practices for seasonal, imbalanced,
  categorical time-series classification: a zero-parameter persistence floor
  reported alongside every headline metric; expanding-window rolling-origin
  cross-validation with embargo, per-fold scaling and sparse-class handling; a
  disqualification rule that rejects interventions which improve an aggregate
  metric while significantly degrading a named safety-critical class; and
  Bonferroni correction over a family of baseline comparisons with the
  resampling resolution floor made explicit. It was extracted from a thesis on
  wearable air-quality forecasting, in which each of the four caught a result
  that the conventional reporting would have presented as a finding.
authors:
  - name: "Md All Shahria"
  - name: "Sanjeda Dewan Mithila"
  - name: "Anik Sarker Rudro"
  - name: "Irfanul Islam Payel"
keywords:
  - time-series classification
  - model evaluation
  - rolling-origin cross-validation
  - walk-forward validation
  - persistence baseline
  - class imbalance
  - conformal prediction
  - air quality
license: MIT
version: 1.0.2
date-released: "2026-09-26"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MD-ALL-SHAHRIA/pulseair"
references:
  - type: generic
    title: "Beijing Multi-Site Air-Quality Data"
    notes: "UCI Machine Learning Repository, id=501. Dataset on which the protocol was developed."
    url: "https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/501/beijing+multi+site+air+quality+data"
